<LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy — Camm Studios" description="How Camm Studios handles website and app data." canonical={new URL('/privacy', Astro.site)} heading="Privacy Policy" updated="August 16, 2026">
  <h2>Overview</h2>
  <p>Camm Studios develops and publishes mobile applications. This policy explains how we handle information across our websites and apps. Each app policy provides the most specific details.</p>
  <h2>Information you provide</h2>
  <p>Some apps ask for profile information to personalize the experience. Depending on the app, this can include a first name, age range, gender, interests, skin type, settings, and preferences.</p>
  <p>Private content such as journal text, custom affirmations, selected photos, progress photos, and vision board content stays on your device unless an app policy says otherwise.</p>
  <h2>Information collected automatically</h2>
  <p>We use service providers to understand app use, manage subscriptions, and measure installs. They may process device details, app version, usage events, purchase status, attribution data, IP based coarse location, and identifiers permitted by your device settings.</p>
  <h2>How we use information</h2>
  <ul><li>Provide, maintain, and personalize our apps.</li><li>Understand feature use and improve performance.</li><li>Manage subscription access.</li><li>Measure installs and campaign performance.</li><li>Protect the reliability and security of our services.</li></ul>
  <h2>Service providers</h2>
  <p>Our apps may use Apple, PostHog, Superwall, RevenueCat, AppsFlyer, and TikTok Events SDK. Our websites use Vercel hosting, Web Analytics, and Speed Insights. These providers process information under their own terms and privacy policies.</p>
  <p>We do not sell personal information for money. Some attribution activity may meet broad legal definitions of sharing or targeted advertising. Device controls, including App Tracking Transparency, can limit supported tracking.</p>
  <h2>Storage and retention</h2>
  <p>On device content stays until you delete it or the app. Service providers retain information under their own retention settings and policies. We use reasonable safeguards, but no system can guarantee complete security.</p>
  <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
  <p>You can control app permissions in iOS settings and delete local content by using app controls or deleting the app. Depending on your location, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, restrict, object, or request a copy of personal information.</p>
  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>Our apps are intended for people aged 18 and over. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children.</p>
  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy and will change the date above. For questions or a privacy request, email <a href="mailto:info@cammstudios.com">info@cammstudios.com</a>.</p>
</LegalLayout>
